# Normalize text files to LF in the repo (matches Netlify's Linux host)
* text=auto eol=lf

# Treat these as binary — never touch line endings
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
# Every catalog set since the responsive-image change has shipped .avif, and
# until now they were binary only because git's own text/binary guess happened
# to spot the NUL bytes. Under `* text=auto eol=lf` that is a guess, not a
# rule, and a wrong guess on a Windows checkout rewrites the bytes.
*.avif binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
